# No trailing slash on purpose: `node_modules/` matches directories only, so a
# SYMLINK named node_modules slipped past it and got committed. Tooling symlinks
# node_modules into scratch worktrees, and a `git add` there stages the link.
node_modules
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Agent working trees. Tooling creates git worktrees here, INSIDE the repo, so `git add -A`
# stages them as embedded repositories and a routine commit can drag another session's whole
# checkout into a public, permanent history. Caught three times by the pre-push scrub; ignored
# now so the scrub is not the only thing standing between a worktree and a publish.
.claude/
